# Skill files are hashed byte-for-byte by verify_skills.py, which compares a
# sha256 over raw disk bytes against registry/skills.lock.json. With
# core.autocrlf=true (the Git for Windows default) and no rule here, checkout
# rewrote every LF to CRLF and all 102 skills reported HASH-MISMATCH on a fresh
# Windows clone. Pinning LF keeps the working tree identical to the locked
# content on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
*.hwpx binary
*.sqlite3 binary
*.zip binary
*.tar.gz binary

# Windows launchers must keep CRLF or cmd.exe misparses them.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
